ls (Borup Fiord area, Northern Ellesmere Island) on July 20, 1978. Debris rich layers have been sheared and folded into the basal cold glacier ice. The glacier front is 6 km broad and up to 40 m high","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEllesmere_Island_05.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Geirangerfjord_%286-2007%29.jpg/500px-Geirangerfjord_%286-2007%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Geirangerfjord_%286-2007%29.jpg/500px-Geirangerfjord_%286-2007%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Differential erosion enhances relief, as clear in this very steep-sided Norwegian fjord.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeirangerfjord_(6-2007).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/TitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg/500px-TitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/TitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg/1280px-TitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/TitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg/500px-TitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ice cracks in the Titlis Glacier","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg"}],"sounds":{"glacier":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9d/En-us-glacier.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9d/En-us-glacier.ogg/En-us-glacier.ogg.mp3"}],"mist":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/49/En-us-mi